-- title:
--   Connected component of a level as formal group p^v-torsion
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel $(p)$, and complete and separated for the $(p)$-adic filtration. Let $h \in \mathbb N$ and let $L$ be a family of commutative rings $L_v$, each a Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra with cocommutative comultiplication and finite free as an $\mathcal O$-module, together with surjective $\mathcal O$-bialgebra maps $t_v \colon L_{v+1} \to L_v$ such that $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O} L_v = p^{vh}$ and $\ker t_v$ is the image of the augmentation ideal $\ker \varepsilon$ of $L_{v+1}$ under the $p^v$-th convolution power of the identity, and such that for every $v$ the Cartier dual $\operatorname{CartierDual}$ of $\mathbb Z/p \otimes_{\mathcal O} L_v$ (its $\mathbb Z/p$-linear dual) is a local ring. Fix $v$. Then there exist a commutative ring $R_0$ that is a Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra, finite and free over $\mathcal O$, a surjective $\mathcal O$-bialgebra map $\rho \colon L_v \to R_0$ and an idempotent $e \in L_v$ with $\varepsilon(e) = 1$, such that the kernel of $\rho$ as an algebra map is $(1-e)$, and $R_0$, $\mathbb Z/p \otimes_{\mathcal O} R_0$ and the Cartier dual of $\mathbb Z/p \otimes_{\mathcal O} R_0$ are all local rings; moreover there exist $d \in \mathbb N$, a $d$-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $\mathcal O$ (that is, $d$ power series in two blocks of $d$ variables with vanishing constant term, identity linear terms and the associativity identity) which is commutative in the sense that interchanging the two blocks fixes each component, and a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi \colon \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]] \to R_0$ such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p) \subseteq R_0$, $\pi$ coincides on every power series with $(p)$-adic evaluation at the tuple $(\pi(X_i))_i$, the kernel of $\pi$ is generated by the components of the $p^v$-multiplication series $[p^v]_F$ (defined by $[0] = 0$ and $[n+1]_F = F([n]_F(X), X)$), and for each $i$ the comultiplication satisfies $\Delta(\pi(X_i)) = F_i(\pi(X)\otimes 1, 1 \otimes \pi(X))$, the right-hand side being the $(p)$-adic evaluation of $F_i$ in $R_0 \otimes_{\mathcal O} R_0$.
--
--   This is the level-$v$ form of the connected–étale decomposition combined with the Tate–Serre correspondence between connected $p$-divisible groups over a complete local ring of residue characteristic $p$ and divisible commutative formal groups: the idempotent $e$ cuts out the connected component of the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} L_v$, whose coordinate ring is the ring of $p^v$-torsion points of a commutative $d$-dimensional formal group law. It feeds the deformation-theoretic statement [`Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp).
